{"kind":"promise","text":"Planner holds G5's operational completion as a separate milestone, open until it is done. This promise is the record. A landing of the G5 Source closes the code request only. It does not close this milestone, and no one calls G5 complete before this promise has its report.\n\nThe milestone starts only after the checker approves the exact final G5 head, and that head is landed on main and pushed. No deployment happens before then. The planner then does these steps, from the clean landed main and pinned tools only:\n1. Deploy the cron Worker that runs the simulator, the /grow/ page, and any host change the runbook names. Set APPLICATION_TRUST to the reviewed trust row, and give the sensors' and the climate agent's keys as secrets.\n2. Found the demo room on the combined cohort (Register17, Directory16, Membership8, Rules10, Destination12), then enrol the two agents, install the signed packet, and create the Site, the Room, four zones and twelve devices, as the runbook says.\n3. Run the runbook's acceptance with a real person. A visitor opens the commissioned room from the homepage. A person takes the operator act through their AI app. Ticks run between visits with no one present.\n\nThe report gives each item on its own line, never merged with the builder's local evidence. The items are: packet release and trust row; custody of the publisher and agent keys; the cohort pins the room was founded with; readbacks of creation, enrolment and install; deployed Worker versions and the cron schedule; the visitor's path; the person's act in the AI app; the tick count between visits. A runbook step that fails goes back to the builder as a new request with what was observed. The planner does not repair it during deployment.","body":{"to":"builder"}}